  "behavior": {
    "detected_audio": "AM envelope, SSB selected real output, and DSB/CW products retain the full IQ input clock until the shared streaming FIR rate converter filters and converts to the device clock. CW beat mixing advances at the actual input clock before filtering.",
    "filters": "Reuse the verified bounded complex FIR decimator and fractional-delay audio FIR. Passband is through 0.4 * min(input Fs, output Fs), transition to 0.5 * min(Fs), with at least 80 dB measured rejection. RF selection runs before detection; detected audio is filtered afterward to remove nonlinear envelope harmonics and CW beat components above audio Nyquist.",
    "controls": "DC removal, CW squelch, audio low-pass, AGC, HPF, notch, shelves and pitch operate at the device clock. Detected envelopes retain DC/headroom greater than full-scale until amplitude controls; RAW stereo clipping semantics remain unchanged.",
    "capture_duration": "Follow the original capture sample count and exact f64 source clock despite preceding RF decimation, tiny blocks and partial RF strides. Native float sample counts are authoritative when an optional byte preview is empty.",
    "constructor": "Initialize source/input clocks consistently at 48 kHz with 1:1 decimation and the 48 kHz audio clock. Capture workers install their real source clock before processing."
  },
